# E §3.1 step 1: "The reality's hash is the sha256 of the UTF-8 bytes of its canonical text, its files reprinted and
# taken in the order of their paths in its directory tree ..., so spacing never changes a hash ... A joint model's use
# line pins a member by this hash"; L §6.1 "A file that doesn't match its hash is refused (LOAD-PIN)". The member is
# pinned by its canonical text's sha256 (refcore's reprint, L §2.4), so the joint model loads and reads a.rate (the
# member's row, 0.12).
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "da53b6ff6a096d47b9af5e16e8276735e72b3c343160d17d841c6ba432df1720"

ask r: a.rate
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"

input rate: num

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  rate = 0.12 "umowa"
=== expect
r: 0.12
  cut 2026-10-20
